course: dictionary
lesson: 9582
title: Stray: lost, or out of place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stray is a word about something being where it should not be. A stray dog is a pet that has wandered off or has no home. A stray sock is one that is away from its pair, in the wrong place.
explain: Stray can describe a thing, name a thing or be a doing word. In «Mercury is hard to spot because it never strays far from the Sun», strays is a doing word: Mercury does not wander far away. The clue is far from the Sun.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. In «Sanjay Gandhi National Park ... has around 50 leopards that hunt stray dogs and rats at night», stray dogs are dogs with no owner or home, not dogs on a lead. Ask yourself: is it lost, or does it have no home?
explain: Safety words matter. Never touch a stray dog. Tell an adult, because a stray may be scared or ill. «Do not stray from the path» means stay on the path. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence.
fact: Stray means wandering away from where it should be, or lost and without a home.
fact: Stray can be an adjective (a stray dog), a noun (a stray) or a verb (to stray).
fact: As a verb, «stray» means to wander away, as in «never strays far from the Sun».
fact: «Stray electricity» is electricity that goes where it should not. The earth pin on a plug gives it a safe path into the ground.
fact: Stray can also mean one thing away from the others, like a stray hair or a stray thought.
exercise: «Mercury ... never strays far from the Sun.» What does strays mean here? | Stays close to | Shines brightly | *Wanders far away | Falls down
exercise: «Donkeys ... will chase away foxes and stray dogs.» What are stray dogs in this sentence? | Dogs that guard the sheep | *Dogs with no owner or home | Dogs that are very clean | Dogs that are asleep
exercise: What is a stray sock? | Made of wool | Very long | Clean and folded in a drawer | *One that is in the wrong place, away from its pair
test: «A stray hair» means one hair that is | hair on a dog | a hair dryer | *out of place, away from the others | a long, healthy hair
test: In safety lessons, what should you do if you see a stray dog? | Chase it home | *Tell an adult and do not touch it | Feed it from your hand | Pick it up and take it inside
exam: «The thick earth pin on a plug gives stray electricity a safe path into the ground.» What does stray electricity mean? | *Electricity that is going where it should not | Electricity from the Sun | A kind of lightning that makes no sound | Electricity that is safe and in its place
